WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>Sandy Island
(The Kingdom of Alabasta)</b>

3
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.220
<b>Sir Crocodile, the Pirate</b>

4
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.730
<b>The Port Town of Nanohana</b>

5
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.320
It's Crocodile!

6
00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.160
He's here to save us!

7
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:25.920
Crocodile?

8
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.500
One of the Seven Warlords?

9
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.750
Thank you, Crocodile!

10
00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.230
It's Crocodile!

11
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.510
Calm down, ignorant peasants.

12
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.470
I only came to your pathetic
little town for that pirate's head.

13
00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:36.960
He's so great!

14
00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.010
And modest!

15
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.430
He comes and saves us,
but he won't take the credit for it!

16
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.350
Three cheers for Crocodile!

17
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.440
The guardian angel of Alabasta!

18
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.440
King of the desert!

19
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.070
Crocodile!

20
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:58.490
<b>Sir Crocodile
One of the Seven Warlords of the Sea
Former Bounty: 81 Million Berries</b>

21
00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.030
You peasants can call me
whatever you want.

22
00:02:59.030 --> 00:02:59.530
But you...

23
00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.370
You pirates should have stayed
out of this country.

24
00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.500
Now you're gonna pay.

25
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.330
Hey, hey, hey, hey! I think
you're underestimating us a bit.

26
00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.960
What, are you gonna take us all on?

27
00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.460
There are a lot of us
and only one of you!

28
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.630
That's right!

29
00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.170
And you're just
the government's little dog.

30
00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.340
Who do you think you are,
acting like a hero?

31
00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.300
For those who wish
to live, lie down now.

32
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.260
What an idiot!
Perfect for target practice.

33
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.100
Get this guy!

34
00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.730
Every last berry in this town is ours.

35
00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.480
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

36
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.240
Nothing but a pathetic puppet!

37
00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.660
No...

38
00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.620
Hm. I'm a puppet, huh?
I don't think so...

39
00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.900
idiot pirate.

40
00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.370
We've been saved!

41
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.290
He's leaving now?

42
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:59.400
– Crocodile! Crocodile!
– Crocodile! Crocodile!

43
00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.910
Looks like he beat us here again.

44
00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:05.910
<b>Alubarna Palace
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

45
00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.910
Seems like he's always
one step ahead.

46
00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.330
By the time we arrived,

47
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.750
the pirates had already
been taken care of.

48
00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.920
I see...

49
00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.830
Well, as long as the citizens are safe,

50
00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.630
I suppose there's no need to worry.

51
00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.630
<b>Nefertari Cobra
King of Alabasta</b>

52
00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.850
Crocodile has been a great help.

53
00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.300
There's no mistaking it.

54
00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:23.760
I hope you're ready!

55
00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.720
We've almost made it to Alabasta.

56
00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.810
Don't lie to me, Luffy!

57
00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.770
Tell me what you know right now.

58
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.650
Don't look away from me.

59
00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.230
I want you to look me in the eyes
right now and tell me the truth.

60
00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.450
No idea what you mean, Sanji.

61
00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.200
I don't know anything! No clue.

62
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.570
Then let me ask you.

63
00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.240
How did enough food
for eight people,

64
00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.330
which I carefully divided up so that
it would last until we reached Alabasta,

65
00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.960
suddenly go missing
in the middle of the night?

66
00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.630
Lying is pointless,
so just tell me the truth.

67
00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.770
You have a terrible poker face.

68
00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.840
Oh, hey, it looks like you have
something around your mouth there.

69
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.260
I forgot about the crumbs!

70
00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.060
I knew it was you!

71
00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.440
Jerk.

72
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.570
Hey, Nami, we need to do something.

73
00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.530
We need a better way of keeping
the food safe from Luffy.

74
00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.240
Can we please buy
a refrigerator that locks?

75
00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.120
Well, maybe.

76
00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.200
Might be a good idea.

77
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.660
Since it could be a matter
of life and death.

78
00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.210
Well, we really do need
to catch something for Sanji.

79
00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.440
So, how's the fishing going?

80
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.470
Uh... well, it's, uh...

81
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:54.730
Pathetic.

82
00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.650
I can't take my eyes off anyone!

83
00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.740
Uh... I'm so hungry...

84
00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.200
And the fish aren't biting at all.

85
00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.370
Really?! You do realize
this is your fault.

86
00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.830
You ate all the bait that we had!

87
00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.960
The fish aren't ever gonna bite
if we don't give them a reason!

88
00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.540
Hey, you ate some too!

89
00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.460
But... I only ate a little bit!

90
00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.000
Just what was stuck to the lid.

91
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.130
Hey, guys! So, how's it going?

92
00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.510
Catch anything yet?

93
00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.140
Karoo?!

94
00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.870
Do you think we could catch a shark?

95
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.480
Don't know. I really
want to catch a sea king.

96
00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.480
Stop fishing with
my duck, you jerks!

97
00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.780
Over there, you two...

98
00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.490
What is that stuff?

99
00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.790
Cotton candy...?

100
00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.430
You guys wait here. I'll go get Nami.

101
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.840
Nami, there's something
wrong! Come quickly!

102
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.840
Oh, yeah, I see it.

103
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.930
Nothing to worry about.
It's just a little steam.

104
00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.470
You're saying that steam's
coming up out of the ocean?

105
00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.890
Uh-huh.
A hot spot, that's all.

106
00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.560
What's a hot spot?

107
00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.690
An area of the sea
where magma's made.

108
00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.620
Below the steam over there
is an undersea volcano.

109
00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.860
There are volcanoes...
underneath the sea?

110
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.450
That's right.

111
00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.280
In fact, there are actually
more volcanoes under the sea

112
00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.780
than there are on dry land.

113
00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.280
Ohhh!

114
00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.290
So, I guess we can't eat
the steam then, huh?

115
00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.810
There'll be a brand-new island
over there, thanks to the volcano.

116
00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.250
But the process will take
tens of thousands of years.

117
00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.380
Oh, wow!

118
00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.250
You're amazing, Nami!

119
00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.010
Wonder if I can live that long.

120
00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.860
I'd plan on dying
sometime before that.

121
00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.720
Have you caught anything?

122
00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.770
We're so hungry.
Can't you cook us something?

123
00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.560
You guys are just hopeless.

124
00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.100
But I'll go search
the storage area anyway

125
00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.910
to see if we have anything left.

126
00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.950
Yuck! It smells like sulfur!

127
00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.200
I can't see anything.
There's steam everywhere...

128
00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.580
Just bear with it. We should
be out of the steam soon!

129
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.210
Excuse me! Mr. 2!

130
00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.250
What is it now?

131
00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.380
There's a whole bunch
of smoke at twelve o'clock!

132
00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.180
I'm not afraid
of some smoke! Keep going!

133
00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.140
Yes, sir! We're going in!

134
00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.720
What is this?

135
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.970
I have no idea.

136
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.980
We made it through!

137
00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.900
Mr. 2 has completely disappeared!

138
00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.900
Let's check the cabin!

139
00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.820
We can't find him!

140
00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.910
This is bad!

141
00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.910
Mr. 2! Where did you go?!

142
00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.790
Now, really!

143
00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.800
This is getting out of hand!

144
00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.760
One of these days, I need to stop
jumping on every random duck I see.

145
00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.220
What is that...?

146
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.140
You have to help me, please!

147
00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.410
Get me out of here,
please! I can't swim!

148
00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.950
I thought I was going to die
there for a minute.

149
00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.370
Hey! You saved me!

150
00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:40.870
Thanks!

151
00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:45.370
"Bon Clay"

152
00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.410
I never imagined
my life would be saved

153
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.370
by a group of complete strangers.

154
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.580
Thanks again.

155
00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.130
I'll never forget your kindness.

156
00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.590
Although, could I trouble you
for a cup of warm soup?

157
00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:52.130
Chicken noodle will do.

158
00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:52.760
– No way!
– No way!

159
00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.420
We can't even feed ourselves!

160
00:10:56.440 --> 00:11:00.060
Oh, hey... You're just
an absolute cutie, aren't you?

161
00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.870
Oh, yeah! Sexy!

162
00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.600
Ugh. He's so weird.

163
00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.850
So, uh... you really can't swim, huh?

164
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.360
That's right! You see,
I ate a devil fruit,

165
00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:10.820
so I can't swim even a little bit.

166
00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.780
Yeah? What kind of fruit?

167
00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.530
Let's see...

168
00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:17.280
Well, since I can't go anywhere
until my ship picks me up,

169
00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.660
there's no harm in a little fun.

170
00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.120
For saving my life, I'll show you.

171
00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.870
Now, get ready.
This is my power!

172
00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.250
What're you–

173
00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.250
Wait, wait.

174
00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.010
Hold on a second!

175
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.920
This is all just
for a little fun, remember?

176
00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.720
Hey now... mean guy! Relax!

177
00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:40.800
Wait!

178
00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:42.560
That's me!

179
00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.640
Fun, fun, fun, fun, fun, fun, fun!

180
00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.230
And if I touch my face
with my left hand...

181
00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.560
I'm back to normal.

182
00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.610
Now that is the power of
the Clone-Clone Devil Fruit, you see.

183
00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:55.570
Amazing...

184
00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:57.570
The body and the voice
match perfectly!

185
00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.760
You, and you, and you, and you!

186
00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.350
Wow! Just wow!

187
00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.080
There! But honestly, I didn't really
have to slap you around like that.

188
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.460
'Kay! Now watch.

189
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.180
All I have to do...

190
00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.750
is touch my right hand to you.

191
00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.090
As you can see, I can mimic anyone.

192
00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:16.630
That's not all. I can change...

193
00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.690
bodies too.

194
00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:22.470
Stop that!

195
00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.780
Uh, guy, are you okay?

196
00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.940
Well, I'm terribly sorry...

197
00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:31.310
but... I shouldn't demonstrate
my power anymore.

198
00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.270
– No, please do more!
– Yeah, yeah!

199
00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.780
Okay! If you absolutely insist,

200
00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.240
I guess I can show a little more!

201
00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.150
Oh, man, that's awesome!

202
00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.110
He's really hamming it up, huh?

203
00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:44.200
Well, in that case, I have
something even more incredible.

204
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.620
I'm equipped with a memory feature!

205
00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.040
– Yeah!
– Yeah, yeah!

206
00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.960
'Kay!

207
00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.540
– Ohh...
– Wow...

208
00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.320
– Oh, wow...
– Whoa...

209
00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.650
Whoa!

210
00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.890
And around and around
and around we go!

211
00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.760
This is just boring.

212
00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.780
And twirl! Open plié.

213
00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.020
Well, did everyone enjoy
my very special secret talent?

214
00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.730
It's quite impressive,
but I almost never show it off!

215
00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:18.030
– Oh, yeah!
– Oh, yeah!

216
00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:22.160
– ♪ It's too good to be true! ♪
– ♪ It's too good to be true! ♪

217
00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.570
Oh, whatever.

218
00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.490
♪ It's too good to be tru-uh-oh! ♪

219
00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.020
♪ It's too good to be true! ♪

220
00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.160
♪ Yeah! ♪

221
00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.880
"Bon Clay"

222
00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.710
It's time to say goodbye already?

223
00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:34.920
What a shame.

224
00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:35.880
– No!
– No!

225
00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.340
No, you can't leave! Please don't go!

226
00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:40.470
Try not to be sad.

227
00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:43.340
Journeys must always
include farewells.

228
00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:46.310
And yet, I will never
forget you or today.

229
00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.640
It's been brief...

230
00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:52.480
but true friendship
isn't determined by time.

231
00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.440
Don't cry, friends!

232
00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:57.400
See you, cool guy!

233
00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.030
Now, quickly, let's be going!

234
00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.360
Yes, sir, Mr. 2! Mr. Bon Clay, sir!

235
00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.750
Mr... 2?!

236
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.580
That guy... is... Mr. 2?

237
00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.250
Vivi! You mean you didn't
know him just by looking?!

238
00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.840
Uh-uh. I've never met Mr. 2
or Mr. 1 and his partner.

239
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.210
I don't know much
about any of them,

240
00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.360
or what their powers may be.

241
00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.180
Though I have heard
rumors about them all.

242
00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.700
I've heard about Mr. 2.

243
00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.980
Apparently, he's a very tall ballerina

244
00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.690
who talks like a woman.

245
00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.230
And he always wears a swan coat.

246
00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.230
The coat says
"Bon Clay" on the back.

247
00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.650
– You didn't know?!
– You didn't know?!

248
00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.240
Is something wrong, Vivi?

249
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.120
I saw something in his memory...

250
00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.450
in the faces that he showed us.

251
00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.210
One of those faces...

252
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.920
belonged to my father!

253
00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.130
Cobra Nefertari...

254
00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.920
my father, the king of Alabasta!

255
00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:01.920
That's not good.

256
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.110
If he can mimic the face
of a king that easily,

257
00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.930
Mr. 2 has the potential
to cause a lot of trouble.

258
00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:09.890
Looks like we let a really bad guy
get away today, huh?

259
00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.220
So, that guy is our enemy?

260
00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:16.190
Seems so, and having him on
the other side is not a good thing.

261
00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:20.730
If Mr. 2 realizes that we're
the ones Baroque Works is after,

262
00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:24.650
then he can use the memories he got
earlier to transform into any one of us!

263
00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.340
We won't even be able
to trust our own friends.

264
00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.370
Really? Uh...

265
00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.130
I'll explain it again.

266
00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.750
No, hold on a sec.

267
00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.580
Luffy's slow, but he's right
not to be scared.

268
00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.170
Just hear me out on this one,
and I think you'll agree.

269
00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.960
It's actually a good thing
that we ran into Mr. 2 when we did,

270
00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.590
because now we can prepare.

271
00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.130
And we can beat him
at his own game.

272
00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:51.400
You sure seem to be in a particularly
good mood for some reason, Mr. 2.

273
00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:50.140
Un, deux, trois...

274
00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.930
how do you say four again?

275
00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.600
It just so happens,
I made some new friends today!

276
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.490
<b>Sea Cat (Sea Monster)
Territory: The Coast of Sandy Island</b>

277
00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.610
That thing is huge!

278
00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.780
A sea cat!

279
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.780
It's a sea monster!

280
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.910
It looks like food to me!

281
00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.290
Yeah! Let's go!

282
00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.830
We're on the right track.

283
00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.840
Now... if we can just
get there alive, that'd be great.

284
00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.670
Food for me!

285
00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.720
It's backing away!

286
00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.840
Reverse! Put the boat in reverse!

287
00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.760
No! We can't do that!

288
00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.020
Hey! Don't let it get away!

289
00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:37.060
If the two of you
don't capture it, I'll kill you!

290
00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.400
Now then, sea kitten!
How do you think I should cook you?

291
00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.460
No!

292
00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.200
Vivi, what are you doing? I'm hungry!

293
00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.660
Why...? Just why? It was food!

294
00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.410
Because you can't eat a sea cat!

295
00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:57.000
I just can't let you!

296
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.330
Sea cats are sacred
animals in Alabasta.

297
00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.370
Well, that's good to know...

298
00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.060
There are more animals
in the ocean than I thought!

299
00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.260
If you're still scared of that stuff,
then you have a long way to go!

300
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.590
So! Let me tell you about
the time that I, Usopp,

301
00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.800
single-handedly fought off the sea kings
of the Calm Belt, young Chopper.

302
00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.180
Sea kings? Really?!

303
00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.850
And big ones too!
Man, they were really huge!

304
00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:20.520
All our food got away!

305
00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.190
Yeah, but don't worry, Luffy.

306
00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.860
You'll be able to stuff
yourself full really soon.

307
00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:28.320
Yeah? Really? Will we get
another cat to eat, Vivi?

308
00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:32.280
Vivi! The wind and weather
seem to be stabilizing.

309
00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:36.160
Uh-huh. We're entering
the climate area of Alabasta island.

310
00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.750
Seeing a sea cat come out
of the water is proof as well.

311
00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.500
And those things you see
behind us over there...

312
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.710
are all the proof I need
that we're getting close.

313
00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.470
That's a lot of ships, huh?
Who are they?

314
00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.270
They're all flying the Baroque Works
symbol on their mast.

315
00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.440
This can't be good.

316
00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.900
It looks as if all the Baroque Works
employees have started gathering.

317
00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.150
I'm guessing that
these are the billions.

318
00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.780
They're the subordinates
under the officer agents.

319
00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:14.030
Which means that there are
at least 200 enemies waiting for us.

320
00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:17.740
The best that Baroque Works has
to offer. The elite of the underlings.

321
00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:21.200
This group will surely be a lot better
than the bounty hunters at Whiskey Peak.

322
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.920
C'mon, let's blow 'em all away!
If we're lucky...

323
00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.420
It'll be quicker if we just
go over there and beat 'em up!

324
00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:30.420
we can get rid of all of them
before they get too close, you know!

325
00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:33.880
Hold on, though.
I need to eat something first.

326
00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.840
Come on, they're not worth it.

327
00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.850
Don't bother.

328
00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:38.310
He's right.

329
00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:41.810
We need to keep our eyes on the prize
or we might lose this altogether.

330
00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.270
After all, 8 against 200 sucks.

331
00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.520
Just make sure and tie it tight.

332
00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.230
I don't want anyone fooled
by the enemy's disguises.

333
00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.530
What a good plan.

334
00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.360
We'll always know
who our friends are.

335
00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.200
Just... look for
the bandage on their arm!

336
00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.450
This Clone-Clone Fruit guy...

337
00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.200
So... is he that similar
when he turns into someone else?

338
00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.460
You have no idea!

339
00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:05.120
It's the same, not just similar!

340
00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.230
It was crazy! Really!

341
00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.840
You shoulda seen it, Sanji.
He changed into every one of us,

342
00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:11.800
even Nami, and then
we got to dance with him!

343
00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:14.670
We know that someone
with his powers is among the enemy,

344
00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.760
so we need to be really careful
to be on our guard at all times.

345
00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.720
So, what should I do to help
against this guy?

346
00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.560
Just do whatever it is you can do.

347
00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.810
You're not expected
to do anything more, Chopper.

348
00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:29.650
And if you get overwhelmed,
then just run.

349
00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.980
Sounds like the pep talk
he's always giving himself.

350
00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.780
Whatever it is I can do...

351
00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.490
I got it!

352
00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.990
I can see the island now!

353
00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.950
Let's stop at the town
called Nanohana.

354
00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.450
We have to hide the ship.

355
00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.330
Okay. No matter what happens
on that island, remember...

356
00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.920
this thing on all our arms...

357
00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.390
is a sign of our friendship.

358
00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.170
Now! Let's land, okay?

359
00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:57.880
Then eat!

360
00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.510
Oh, and help Vivi.

361
00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.180
– That's a side note?
– That's a side note?

362
00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.640
Now, remember, our enemy
is a whole gang of assassins.

363
00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.020
Uh, yeah. Sure is.

364
00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.230
Just try to think before
you do anything stupid,

365
00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.110
you got that?

366
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.400
Yeah, of course.

367
00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:13.440
You're right. I got it.

368
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.030
No, really, I will!

369
00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.090
I promise!

370
00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.620
<b>The Port of Nanohana,
The Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

371
00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:20.450
Hey, what happened?

372
00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:21.800
What's everybody looking at?

373
00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:26.120
I don't know. They said some guy just
dropped dead sitting up at the counter.

374
00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.460
Our food's never been
that bad before.

375
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.210
What's going on? What happened?

376
00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.920
Well... someone died.

377
00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.590
Apparently, he suddenly dropped dead
right in the middle of the restaurant.

378
00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:37.670
He just died?!

379
00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:42.010
Yeah, he just up and keeled over
during a conversation with the owner.

380
00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.560
He isn't from here.

381
00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.850
We think he may have accidentally
eaten a desert strawberry while traveling,

382
00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.100
not knowing what it was.

383
00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.400
Uh, what is a desert strawberry?

384
00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.810
There's a species
of poisonous spiders

385
00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.280
that look like red strawberries
growing in the desert.

386
00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.990
Anyone who eats one
will suddenly die a few days later.

387
00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.880
The infection spreads
throughout the corpse,

388
00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.370
and it's contagious,
so no one can go near.

389
00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.680
It's a quick but unpleasant way to go.

390
00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:08.080
You have to be careful in the desert.

391
00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.200
Anything you touch can kill you.

392
00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.520
But just look at the way his arm
is still stuck up like that,

393
00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.380
holding on to a bite of meat.

394
00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:17.760
That's proof of just how swiftly
the desert strawberry acts.

395
00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:19.770
It's an incredibly deadly creature.

396
00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.140
He came back to life!

397
00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:34.520
Um... are you all right?

398
00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:40.780
Ah... Sorry about that.

399
00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.780
Fell asleep.

400
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.910
– You were asleep?!
– You were asleep?!

401
00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:46.280
That doesn't make sense!

402
00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.500
You were right in the middle
of a conversation!

403
00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.620
And now you're just eating
like nothing happened?!

404
00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.580
Jeez, what's all
the commotion about, anyway?

405
00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:57.340
We thought you had dropped dead!
Are you crazy?!

406
00:21:57.340 --> 00:22:00.470
Does this restaurant of yours
do comedy skits or something?

407
00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:03.220
Nope. That isn't our thing, not here.

408
00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.030
We're just glad that you're all right.

409
00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:08.060
– Damn it! Cut it out!
– Damn it! Cut it out!

410
00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:13.600
Every time he falls asleep
 someone thinks he's dead.

411
00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:14.770
So, it turns out
he wasn't dead after all?

412
00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:27.300
Yeah, I think that oughta do it.

413
00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:28.790
Tell me, mister.

414
00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:30.080
What is it?

415
00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:32.080
Have you by any chance
seen this guy?

416
00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:34.710
He's a pirate that wears a straw hat.

417
00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:38.920
You've got some nerve, eating in
the middle of a public place like this.

418
00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:42.630
Even for a division commander
of the Whitebeard Pirates.

419
00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:47.800
<b>Commander Portgas D. Ace
Second Division
Whitebeard Pirates</b>

420
00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:47.800
Hello, Portgas D. Ace.

421
00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.180
Huh? No way!
Not the Whitebeard Pirates!

422
00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:54.640
I knew I'd seen that mark
on his back before!

423
00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:57.400
You mean this weirdo is
one of the Whitebeard Pirates?

424
00:22:57.400 --> 00:22:59.290
It's the mark
of the Whitebeard Pirates!

425
00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:00.830
But what is he doing here?

426
00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:04.070
I'm curious.

427
00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:06.660
What's such a big-shot pirate
doing in this country?

428
00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:14.220
I'm looking for someone.

429
00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:19.170
My little brother.
